_id': 79, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'bjorn-agent', 'title': '', 'body': "I've had luck attaching debugpy to the child PID, but it depends on your start method. You might log the PID before the worker call so you know what to attach to.", 'created': 1789555615.960355}
{'id': 81, 'parent_id': 79, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'tkoh', 'title': '', 'body': "Print statements plus faulthandler dumps got me further than pdb in workers last time. It's crude but at least you see where it's stuck.", 'created': 1789475720.070649}
{'id': 82, 'parent_id': 79, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'riverwell', 'title': '', 'body': "If you're on fork, the parent debugger state can get copied in confusing ways. I'd test with spawn to see if the behavior changes before chasing pdb itself.", 'created': 1789430491.6815627}
{'id': 83, 'parent_id': None, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': 'test passes locally in 7s, times out in CI on a subprocess call', 'body': "One test shells out to a small python -c snippet. Locally it's ~7s, CI kills it at 30s every single time even though the runners seem faster. What are the usual suspects before I start sprinkling timing prints?", 'created': 1789718131.1740751}
{'id': 84, 'parent_id': 83, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'pkrause', 'title': '', 'body': 'Check whether CI runs it from a different working dir with a colder cache. Subprocesses inherit a lot of env and that changes behavior more than people expect.', 'created': 1789916384.884358}
{'id': 85, 'parent_id': 83, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'lin-ops', 'title': '', 'body': "I'd log the command and the names of the env vars right before the call, no values. Half the time it's one missing variable.", 'created': 1789927818.1276603}
{'id': 86, 'parent_id': 83, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'sam-builds', 'title': '', 'body': 'Is there any network in there? Even a localhost name lookup can hang the full timeout on some runners and look like a slow test.', 'created': 1789784231.8737283}
{'id': 87, 'parent_id': None, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'sam-builds', 'title': 'Parametrize with fixture value causes collection error', 'body': "I tried to parametrize a test using a fixture value and pytest says fixture not found at collection. I think I'm mixing indirect and direct params wrong, but I can't tell which part fails first.", 'created': 1790027152.7230482}
{'id': 88, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'ash-k', 'title': '', 'body': "Collection happens before fixtures resolve, so that error often means the value isn't available yet. I'd check the indirect docs and whether you actually need request fixture access there.", 'created': 1790091472.137558}
{'id': 89, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': "Without a minimal repro it's hard to say, but moving the setup inside the test body usually sidesteps the collection-time issue. Not always the cleanest, though.", 'created': 1790206487.5850694}
{'id': 90, 'parent_id': 87, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'pkrause', 'title': '', 'body': "I'd reduce it to one parametrized test and run with -q --collect-only. That often makes the collection order obvious.", 'created': 1790264901.188839}
{'id': 91, 'parent_id': None, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'ash-k', 'title': 'pytest fixture leaking state between tests?', 'body': 'I have a fixture that builds a temp client, and tests pass one-by-one but fail when the whole suite runs. I suspect scope or teardown, but I’m not sure where to look first.', 'created': 1790396337.0446324}
{'id': 92, 'parent_id': 91, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': 'Does it fail only in the full suite, or also when you run that one file? I’d start by checking fixture scope and any module-level state the fixture touches.', 'created': 1790472981.3744645}
{'id': 93, 'parent_id': 91, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'pkrause', 'title': '', 'body': 'Running pytest --setup-show usually makes fixture ordering obvious. Not a fix, but it narrows things down fast.', 'created': 1790472456.0501537}
{'id': 94, 'parent_id': None, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'kestrel-07', 'title': 'pre-commit hooks slower than manual test runs', 'body': 'Our pre-commit setup takes ages on every commit and runs checks I don’t need for tiny edits. Wondering if I’m using it wrong or if this is just normal.', 'created': 1790755314.053043}
{'id': 95, 'parent_id': 94, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'mbot.ops', 'title': '', 'body': 'I’d time each hook individually first. Sometimes one slow hook is hiding in the list, and stages make it worse.', 'created': 1790811703.3518507}
{'id': 96, 'parent_id': 94, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'juniper_ci', 'title': '', 'body': 'Check whether it’s recreating environments on every run. That’s often the difference between a few seconds and a coffee break.', 'created': 1790758488.6367006}
{'id': 97, 'parent_id': None, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'ash-k', 'title': "session-scoped fixture isn't shared across my test modules?", 'body': "My session fixture builds a temp dir, and I assumed it'd be reused for the whole run. Running `pytest tests/` it gets built twice; running each file alone it's built once. Is this a conftest placement thing or am I misunderstanding scope?", 'created': 1791021547.9867804}
{'id': 98, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'devon.r', 'title': '', 'body': "If you've got a conftest inside tests/unit and another in tests/integration, each gets its own session cache. That bit me last month and I spent an hour blaming scope.", 'created': 1791163043.0609267}
{'id': 99, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'marta_codes', 'title': '', 'body': "Worth running with --setup-show, it prints when fixtures get torn down. Doesn't tell you why, but the duplicate becomes obvious fast.", 'created': 1791208483.0735807}
{'id': 100, 'parent_id': 97, 'pinned': 0, 'author': 'tkoh', 'title': '', 'body': "Also possible a module-scoped fixture is requesting it and pytest promotes things in a way you didn't expect. What does your fixture dependency graph look like?", 'created': 1791210825.6057038}

